You can read WP stories on your Kindle by downloading them as EPUB and using Amazon's free Send-to-Kindle service. Here's the full process.

## What you need

- A WP story URL
- An Amazon account with a Kindle device or the Kindle app
- Your Kindle email address (found in Amazon settings)

## Step 1: Download the story as EPUB

1. Copy the story URL from the Wattpad website or app.
2. Go to [WP Downloader](/) and paste the URL.
3. Make sure **EPUB** is selected as the format (it's the default - no sign-in needed).
4. Click **Download** and save the EPUB file.

## Step 2: Find your Kindle email address

1. Go to Amazon's "Manage Your Content and Devices" page.
2. Click **Preferences**.
3. Scroll to **Personal Document Settings**.
4. Find the **Send-to-Kindle Email** address for your device (it ends in `@kindle.com`).

If you use the Kindle app, each device (phone, tablet) has its own address. Pick the one you want to read on.

## Step 3: Send the EPUB to your Kindle

**Option A - Email:**
1. Open your email app and create a new email.
2. In the To field, enter your Kindle email address.
3. Attach the EPUB file and send. (The subject line doesn't matter.)
4. Amazon converts and delivers the book to your Kindle within minutes.

**Option B - Send-to-Kindle app (Windows/Mac):**
1. Download the Send-to-Kindle desktop app from Amazon.
2. Drag and drop the EPUB file onto the app window.
3. Select your Kindle device and click Send.

## Step 4: Read on your Kindle

The story will appear in your Kindle library automatically. If it doesn't show up after a few minutes, open the Kindle library and sync manually.

## Tips

- **File size**: Most WP story EPUBs are well under Amazon's 50 MB email limit.
- **Images**: Enable the Include Images toggle in WP Downloader if you want chapter images to appear on your Kindle.
- **Series**: Download each book individually and send them all - they'll appear in your library in order.

## Troubleshooting

**Email not arriving** - check that your sending address is on Amazon's approved senders list under Personal Document Settings. Add your email address if it isn't there.

**File rejected** - make sure the file is under 50 MB and is in EPUB format.

**Book doesn't sync** - manually sync your Kindle by going to the home screen and pulling down to refresh, or tap Menu → Sync.
